{
  "id": "afl",
  "name": "AFL",
  "description": "Deep navy chrome with a red accent; dark mode is a navy surface ramp rather than neutral gray. Links, buttons and nav fills keep the blue primary.",
  "notes": {
    "--afl-gold": "Amber accent for championship hero tints and borders. Not the badge gold - use --afl-trophy-gold to match award art.",
    "--afl-gold-text": "Gold as FOREGROUND. --afl-gold is 3.2:1 on a white card and --afl-trophy-gold 2.4:1, both under AA; this is 5.0:1. Dark flips to the metallic badge gold (6.3:1 on the navy card).",
    "--color-primary": "Deliberately the shared blue in both modes: it feeds FILLS (nav active pill, buttons, focus rings), where a white value would be white-on-white.",
    "--link-color": "Dark: headings and plain anchors go white with a red hover, so red stays the accent and not the body voice.",
    "--cta-fill": "The CTA fill is the league accent. Light: red #c41e3a carries white at 5.84:1. Dark: the accent #ef5350 carries white at only 3.49:1, so the fill is the deeper #d81b41 (5.06:1, MFL Live's dark button red); hover #e02a4d is 4.56:1.",
    "--color-primary-fill": "Primary as a FILL under text (pills, chips, active nav). Dark: --color-primary #3b82f6 is the TEXT blue (4.07:1 on the navy card) and carries white at only 3.68:1; the fill is #2563eb, white 5.17:1, the dark primary button's blue. Unset = fills use --color-primary.",
    "--on-league-accent": "Text ON a --league-accent fill: white where white clears AA on the accent, near-black where it does not (a bright dark-mode accent carries white at under 4.5:1).",
    "--hero-surface": "The AFL's hero chrome is its navy #002244 in BOTH modes (the branded event card, the schedule hero), with a red glow and gold highlight."
  },
